        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport, Louisville International Airport, Staunton, Augusta County, Virginia, Louisville, Jefferson County, Kentucky, United States\n- Systems: IATA, ICAO, FAA LID\n- Topics: airport location, airport use, commercial airline service\n\nFacts:\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport has the codes IATA SHD, ICAO KSHD, and FAA LID SHD.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport is a public airport located 10 nautical miles northeast of the central business district of Staunton in Augusta County, Virginia, United States.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport is used mostly for general aviation and is also served by one commercial airline.\n- Louisville International Airport has the codes IATA SDF, ICAO KSDF, and FAA LID SDF.\n- Louisville International Airport is a public and military-use public airport centrally located in Louisville in Jefferson County, Kentucky, United States.",
